      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROYAL SCRIPTURE (3) was much better third-up in town when sticking on gamely into a close fifth after riding the early speed. Finds an easier assignment and gets in well with the 2kg claimer taking over. Top hope. HE'S A COOL CAT (1) also drops back in grade and is ticking along nicely. Made light work of his rivals two back before following up with a good midfield finish on the Parks track last time. The extra 200m should suit fourth-up and looks the obvious danger. PRODIGAL LAD (2) got things back on track at the latest when rattling home in to placings at Murray Bridge after straightening near the tail of the field. Is a genuine hope if he keeps the ball rolling. PRINCE KURO (5) showed early speed from an outside draw last time and led for much of the way before fading to finish fifth, only beaten 1.4L. Is sure to spear across from the wide gate and give backers another bold sight.",
